    "notes": "The AIR only: Weatherly's Danny Boy lyric (1913) is a separate work and is not carried. Set here in 3/4 after Gilchrist's triple-time reading (JEFDSS, 1934): quarter-note pulse, 3 beats per bar; every pitch and every eighth-note figure follows the 1855 air, with phrase-end holds shortened by one beat to fit triple meter. Transposed to C. The chorus tail carries the verse pickup (7-1-2) as a turnaround; the outro grounds it when the form ends. Confidence medium: the A strain and the B-strain structure (pickups, phrase ends, single 3' peak) are verified; B-strain ornament-level detail rests on the editorial triple-time reading."
